{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And you shall strengthen him.</b> Do not let him descend and fall, so that it becomes hard to raise him up — rather, strengthen him from the moment his hand falters. To what is this likened? To a burden on a donkey: while it is still on the donkey, one person can grab it and hold it steady; once it has fallen to the ground, five cannot raise it up." "<b>A ger and toshav.</b> Even if he is a ger or a toshav. And who is a toshav? Anyone who has accepted upon himself not to worship idolatry and [yet] eats nevelot (see Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:23.465652466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}